Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 30 04:50:00 2026 +0000

    Convert two edfringe-data prose rules to checks

    Prose-to-checks sweep over the repo's own local packs. Both rules were
    always-testable and only ever lived as prose in edfringe-data/RULES.md.

    edfringe-ticket-status-unavailable (blocking)
      Every availability denylist in the front-end code must deny
      NO_ALLOCATION_CONTACT_VENUE alongside SOLD_OUT. A performance can be
      soldOut: false with no online allocation left, so a denylist naming only
      SOLD_OUT renders those shows as buyable. Scoped parse of `new Set([...])`
      literals rather than a grep — plan/plan.js names the same statuses in
      colour/label switch arms, and flagging those would be a false alarm.

    edfringe-normalizer-selftest-in-verify (blocking)
      scripts/verify.sh must actually invoke `scraper/normalize.py --selftest`.
      The live API is unreachable from a session, so this is the ONE transform
      check that runs offline; drop it and scraper changes ship unverified. The
      check strips `step "..."` labels and comments before looking, because
      verify.sh's own step heading quotes the command — a plain grep would pass
      a gutted script.

    See-it-fail: both live-gate tests were confirmed red against mutated real
    repo content (js/app.js denylist shrunk; the verify.sh invocation replaced
    by an echo, leaving the label) and green again after revert.

    Prose trimmed to rationale in edfringe-data/RULES.md; enforcement now points
    at the checks. Full gate green: bash scripts/verify.sh, 150 tests passing.

    Part of #170

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01V3Rq7t9LbH87wYFbN4q64q

 .claudinite/local/packs/edfringe-data/RULES.md     |  23 ++-
 .../normalizer-selftest-in-verify.mjs              |  57 +++++++
 .claudinite/local/packs/edfringe-data/pack.mjs     |   4 +-
 .../local/packs/edfringe-data/pack.test.mjs        | 182 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 .../edfringe-data/ticket-status-unavailable.mjs    |  74 +++++++++
 5 files changed, 331 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
=== ticket-status-unavailable.mjs ===
// Dependency-free by design: a local pack's checks must load without the
// vendored mount, so this returns plain finding objects rather than importing
// engine/checks/helpers/findings.mjs.

// "Can I get a ticket" comes from the per-performance `ticketStatus`, and two
// statuses mean no: the obvious `SOLD_OUT`, and `NO_ALLOCATION_CONTACT_VENUE` —
// nothing left to sell online even though `soldOut` is false. Every availability
// denylist in the front-end code must carry BOTH; a list that has only SOLD_OUT
// is the exact bug this rule exists to stop.
const SOLD_OUT = 'SOLD_OUT';
const NO_ALLOCATION = 'NO_ALLOCATION_CONTACT_VENUE';

// The front-end source the availability decision is made in. Test fixtures
// deliberately construct partial status sets, and plan/design/ is a static HTML
// mock, so neither is this rule's business.
const SOURCE = /^(js|plan|shared)\/.*\.m?js$/;
const NOT_SOURCE = (f) => f.includes('/__tests__/') || f.startsWith('plan/design/');

// Scoped parse rather than a grep: `NO_ALLOCATION_CONTACT_VENUE` appears all over
// plan/plan.js in switch arms that pick a colour and a label, and flagging those
// would be a false alarm. The rule means the *denylist* — a `new Set([...])` of
// status literals — so find those and read their elements. A Set whose elements
// include SOLD_OUT is an availability denylist by construction; anything else in
// the file is left alone.
const SET_LITERAL = /new Set\(\s*\[([^\]]*)\]\s*\)/g;

/** The string literals of a flat array body, with line comments stripped first
 *  (an apostrophe inside a `// you'd have to…` comment is not a quote). */
function elementsOf(body) {
  const code = body.replace(/\/\/[^\n]*/g, '');
  return [...code.matchAll(/["'`]([^"'`]*)["'`]/g)].map((m) => m[1]);
}

const rule = {
  id: 'edfringe-ticket-status-unavailable',
  severity: 'blocking',
  description:
    'Every availability denylist in the front-end code treats NO_ALLOCATION_CONTACT_VENUE as unavailable alongside SOLD_OUT',
  why:
    'a performance can be soldOut: false and still have nothing to sell online (NO_ALLOCATION_CONTACT_VENUE) — a denylist that names only SOLD_OUT renders those shows as buyable, sending people to a basket that cannot take them',
  doc: 'RULES.md',

  run(ctx) {
    const out = [];

    for (const file of ctx.files.filter((f) => SOURCE.test(f) && !NOT_SOURCE(f)).sort()) {
      const text = ctx.read(file);
      if (text === null) continue;

      SET_LITERAL.lastIndex = 0;
      for (const m of text.matchAll(SET_LITERAL)) {
        const elements = elementsOf(m[1]);
        // Not a status denylist unless it denies the obvious one.
        if (!elements.includes(SOLD_OUT)) continue;
        if (elements.includes(NO_ALLOCATION)) continue;

        out.push({
          rule: rule.id,
          severity: rule.severity,
          file,
          line: text.slice(0, m.index).split('\n').length,
          what: `this availability denylist lists ${SOLD_OUT} but not ${NO_ALLOCATION}`,
          why: rule.why,
          fix: `add "${NO_ALLOCATION}" to the set — availability keys off ticketStatus, and that status means the online allocation is gone even when soldOut is false`,
          doc: rule.doc,
        });
      }
    }

    return out;
  },
};

export default rule;

